      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! Here\u0027s the answer from the wiki:\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **Injection into child processes only**: The key is injected directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s process environment is never mutated** \u2014 the key never exists in the Hub\u0027s own environment at all\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables. The key exists only inside the short-lived child process (either the Ingest or Query agent) that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.",
